{
 "pass": "Ballotpedia #Campaign_themes anchors that lead to no candidate words (2026-10-08)",
 "why": "The CI gate carves a deep-linked #Campaign_themes citation out of BALLOTPEDIA_ONLY, and the generic-sourcing detectors now classify it as the candidate speaking rather than as a generic page. Both tests are on the URL, because neither can fetch. Fetching all 160 pages the corpus deep-links showed the URL test is right about roughly nine rows in ten and wrong about the rest: 84 pages carry real survey answers, 57 carry no survey but a verbatim quote of the candidate’s own campaign website under the same heading, and the 19 pages listed here carry neither. Rows citing them look like the remedy the gate asks for while the page says nothing.",
 "not_a_delete_list": "A reading queue. The claim in each row may still be true and sourceable elsewhere; what is established is only that the cited page does not carry it.",
 "method": "Fetched each distinct page with a browser user-agent, took the text of the section introduced by id=\"Campaign_themes\" up to the next h2, and applied two tests: the NO_SURVEY_NOTICE pattern from scripts/lib/candidate-connection.mjs, and whether Ballotpedia frames the section as a quote of the campaign website. ⚠ Ballotpedia answers 202 to a fast sweep; 122 of the first 160 requests were rate-limited and had to be re-fetched at one every three seconds. A 202 is a challenge, not an absent page.",
 "counts": {
  "pages": 19,
  "rows": 58,
  "rows_with_a_non_zero_chair": 50,
  "corpus_pages_deep_linked": 160,
  "corpus_pages_with_survey_answers": 84,
  "corpus_pages_quoting_the_campaign_site": 57
 },
